===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʷreh₂-|*-mn̥}}
{{lbor|en|LL.|gravāmen|t=physical inconvenience}} and {{der|en|ML.|gravāmen|t=grievance}}, from {{der|en|la|gravāre}} + {{m|la|-men|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|neuter}} {{glossary|noun}}s of the third {{glossary|declension}}}}. {{m|la||Gravāre}} is the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|active}} {{glossary|infinitive}} of {{m|la|gravō|t=to burden, weigh down; to oppress}}, from {{m|la|gravis|t=heavy; grave, serious; hard, troublesome}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gʷreh₂-|t=heavy}}) + {{m|la|-ō|pos=suffix forming regular first-{{glossary|conjugation}} {{glossary|verb}}s}}.<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=80985|date=December 2019|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref>

The {{glossary|plural}} form {{m|en|gravamina}} is derived from {{der|en|LL.|gravāmina}}.

