===Noun===
{{en-noun|+|gravamina}}

# A [[grievance]] [[complain]]ed of.
# The [[essence]] or [[ground#Noun|ground]] of a [[complaint]].
#* '''1822''', [http://books.google.co.uk/books?id=T5A-AAAAYAAJ&pg=PA903 ''The Annual Register, or a view of the History, Politics, and Literature, of the year 1820'', part II, Abstracts of State Trials], account of trial following the [[w:Peterloo Massacre|Peterloo Massacre]], pages 902–903:
#*: Falsehood, which was in ordinary cases the '''''gravamen''''' of the complaint, was omitted altogether in the information against him.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} The essence or [[most#Determiner|most]] [[important]] [[aspect]] of a [[piece#Noun|piece]] of [[writing#Noun|writing]], a [[point#Noun|point]] of [[argument#Noun|argument]], etc.; the [[gist#Noun|gist]].
#: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:essence}}
#* '''2002''', Eric S. Raymond, [http://www.catb.org/~esr/sf-words/essay.html ''SF Words and Prototype Worlds'']:
#*: The '''gravamen''' of this essay is that these signifiers (the jargon of SF) function not merely as a set of isolated signs {{...}}
# {{lb|en|Anglicanism}} A [[document#Noun|document]] [[send|sent]] by the [[lower#Adjective|Lower]] [[house#Noun|House]] of [[convocation|Convocation]] to the [[upper#Adjective|Upper]] House to [[inform]] the [[latter]] of [[certain#Determiner|certain]] grievances in the [[church#Noun|church]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[formal#Adjective|formal]] [[charge#Noun|charge]] or complaint.

